From 47d834252aaee3fb6c546c024c5931728dcf45cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:34:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sim): one eikonal sweep re-normalizes the render
 lattice's band

FieldLattice::renormalize runs one cycle of fast sweeping (Zhao 2005:
Godunov upwind update, Gauss-Seidel over the eight sweep orders) over
the packed lattice's narrow band, so the sphere-traced view's shading
gradient reads |grad phi| ~ 1 where the BFS magnitudes and the cut
layer's CSG max leave it bent. PackedBase::of calls it before the
render pass's upload.

- The surface never moves: every texel with a 26-neighbour of the
  other sign is frozen bit for bit, every other texel keeps its sign.
- Band only: texels at or past cap are untouched; solved magnitudes
  clamp at cap. Cost is 8 x band texels updates, deterministic.
- The cut layer stays as packed (the composed value goes into the mesh
  layer), so playback's later cut layers only lift cells over it.
- Display only: the verdict paths keep reading the sparse field.

Pinned by tests/stock_eikonal.rs: CSG cuts' mean | |grad| - 1 | drops
0.367 -> 0.048 (bound 0.08, 83% of texels within 0.1); every texel
keeps its sign and every zero-crossing edge keeps both values; a
cylinder pocket agrees with its closed-form distance within 0.21 at a
0.5 cell; a plane reads exact; out-of-band texels untouched;
deterministic; a mismatched lattice refuses unchanged.

Fixes #22

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
